"P181904886" "No More Fears"
// flashbackteamrequiresfailedtext :
"P1881094247" "You and everyone on your team must not have Officer Fields' story arc as an active arc, must have completed Matthew Habashy's arc, and be over level 7 to begin his flashback."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Witness3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3068912893" "The Vahzilok Murders"
// DetailString :
"P1921311693" "The witness at the crime scene told you about a gruesome scene, in which the Vahzilok killed Larry Botte, took his kidney, then retreated back to a nearby sewer system."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - VahzilokPlans 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2565652159" "A Gathering of Parts"
// DetailString :
"P1789271893" "You fought off a group of Vahzilok in the sewers and found a document titled, 'List of attendees'. It looks to be a list of the people attending the charity play in the Promenade, including the actors!<br><br>Next to each of their names is a body part, presumably the one that the Vahzilok are after."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AskHelp 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P840108946" "Victoria Manuel's Decline"
// DetailString :
"P1886931598" "You asked Victoria Manuel to help you with the Vahzilok problem, but she declined, saying that you would be better off handling the situation."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - VahzilokPlot 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1653966479" "Examining the Bodies"
// DetailString :
"P4079619995" "After fighting with the Vahzilok in the streets of Paragon, you discovered one of them had a hand-written note from Dr. Vahzilok himself...<br><br>'Botte will be the first to be tested. Those who have survived the Galaxy Incident will have, undoubtedly, been exposed in some way to the Shivans or to the meteors.<br><br>We must see what effects this can have on the human person, and if possible, how it can be used to improve our current procedures. Report everything you find to Botte.<br><br>Dr. Vahzilok.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL1_OfficerNelson 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2473056875" "Lifetime Movie Pass"
// tDetailString :
"P3725720055" "You received this lifetime movie pass to the movie theater in Atlas Park after defending it from the Vahzilok. It reminds you of a series of event you've come to know as...<br><br><b>No More Fears</b><br><br>It all started when Matthew Habashy introduced you to Officer Fields, a PPD recruit from Galaxy City who needed help with a murder case in the Promenade. You went to the crime scene and found out that there were some witnesses who saw what happened, but were too afraid to speak up, believing that the PPD was unable to protect them. You convinced the witness that you and the PPD could keep her safe and discovered that the murder was carried out by the Vahzilok. You went into one of their lairs in the sewers to clear them out and found the Vahzilok were going to be targeting people attending a charity play in the Promenade!<br><br>You immediately went to the movie theater to warn the manager, Victoria Manuel, about the dangers. She seemed to be confident in your abilities to handle the situation on your own, despite the fact that <i>she</i> herself was super-powered and could help you. Regardless, you were off to push back the Vahzilok nearby and found a note from Dr. Vahzilok himself. It seems that the Vahzilok were targeting people who had survived the Galaxy Incident, believing that there was something special about being exposed to the Shivan meteors and that a man named Botte was handling everything going on. Officer Fields believed this to be a man named Joseph Botte, the brother of the man who was previously killed.<br><br>Fields provided you with the location of where Botte may be located, along with the people who have already been kidnapped. You stormed the sewers and rescued the hostages before the Vahzilok could carve them up. You then confronted Joseph Botte, who revealed his motives behind all of this: he was simply afraid, and Dr. Vahzilok promised him a way to immortality, a life where he wouldn't have to be afraid anymore. You put a stop to Botte's operation, saving the Promenade from the mad schemes of Dr. Vahzilok.<br><br>Officer Fields thanked you for all your help and believed this was the last of the problems in the Promenade. Looking back, the real source of all these problems was Dr. Vahzilok; he preyed on the fears of the people, using them for his own scientific ends. You have to wonder, did he even care to alleviate the fears of Botte and the others who survived the Galaxy Incident, or was this all just being done in the name of his own mad scientific research?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Witness1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2448203106" "I told them I'm not saying anything, just standing here will make me a tar - <br><br>Wait... you're {HeroName}, aren't you? The one who stopped the Hellions! Do you think... would you be able to handle what's going on here? That you'll protect me from the people who did this?"
// Answer Text :
"P2665182826" "I will. Just tell me what happened."
// Page NextPage Text :
"P1696611217" "I was out here this morning when I saw that man being chased by the <color yellow>Vahzilok</color>! They yelled that they couldn't let his 'parts' get away. I hid behind a dumpster and watched as they killed him, then took his kidney! It... it was horrible!<br><br>There were a few of them, they said that this, 'would do nicely', and that it was time to bring the parts back to the 'guest'!<br><br>They went into the <color yellow>sewers</color> nearby. {HeroName}, you have to find out what's going on! I don't want to be their next victim, I just want to be safe!"
// Answer Text :
"P3906751258" "Don't worry, I'll get to the bottom of this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3626001939" "Well, we've got a murder case on our hands. <color yellow>Larry Botte</color>, an actor known throughout the Promenade, was found dead in front of a nearby office complex. The real shame is that his brother, <color yellow>Joseph Botte</color>, has also gone missing since the meteors hit Galaxy.<br><br>I was going to investigate it myself, see if there was any connection, but, well, I still get kind of sick around bodies. I haven't formed that hardened cop fortitude yet.<br><br><i>But</i> I <i>was</i> top in my class, {HeroName}, and I can smell something bigger brewing here. And I don't like it one bit."
// AcceptString :
"P2385045568" "Well... what are you 'smelling'?"
// SendOffString :
"P1354811197" "Larry was playing a big role in a <color yellow>charity play being put on for victims of the Galaxy Incident.</color><br><br>I think someone doesn't want that event to go off. The one thing that bugs me is <i>why</i>, who would want to stop something that's just trying to <i>help</i> people.<br><br>Anyway, you should go <color yellow>speak with Detective Pierce and investigate the crime scene.</color> I'll be here following up on any leads that might arise."
// TaskTitle :
"P2687847718" "<color deepskyblue>No More Fears</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P344869121" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: The List</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3887271152" "Speak with Detective Pierce"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P316506549" "Nothing here on my end so far, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P808644395" "{HeroName}, heard about you from Fields. Sure wish they'd give us something more here than the fresh recruits, but eh, what're you going to do?<br><br>We've got our victim over here. It looks like he was trying to run away from something or someone after being badly injured. Whoever did this delivered a killing blow, took out one of his <color yellow>kidneys</color>, and then left.<br><br>We've got a witness here, but she's refusing to answer us. She's saying that we can't protect her if she talks. No more faith and all that. Maybe if a hero talks to her, she'll think differently. Can you give it a shot?"

